  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q19-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "The perimeter of a rectangle is 40 cm and its area is 84 cm². Let its width be $x$.\nWrite a quadratic equation using this information and find the rectangle’s dimensions.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^2-20x+84=0$. Factorising gives $(x-6)(x-14)=0$, so the dimensions are 14 cm by 6 cm.",
      "worked": "Let the length be $y$ cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2y&=40\\\\y&=20-x\\\\A&=xy\\\\84&=x(20-x)\\\\x^2-20x+84&=0\\\\(x-6)(x-14)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nBy the null factor law, $x=6$ or $x=14$. The corresponding other dimension is $14$ cm or $6$ cm, respectively. Both roots describe the same rectangle: 14 cm by 6 cm.\nCheck: $2(14+6)=40$ cm and $14\\times6=84$ cm².",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 85
  },
